From 43d5052cfd43966806d0b74bb9b43b8e49789e39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:43:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): review of the wake-reason change: guidance,
 blocker and clock waits, goal parks [daveey]

- Guidance that still taught bare parks (worker prompt, supervisor-request next_step, goal-mode refusal, tool
  schemas, create-args, done-tail, continue/background hints, kanban docs) now names the wake reason (awaiting).
- A shared blocker is a wake reason: gate threads blocker_id into resolve/_infer; a park behind a named blocker
  with nothing else records {kind:'external', ref:'shared blocker <id>', why, shared_blocker} (no escalation).
- Declared clock waits with no wake probe never escalate (a clock is its own producer); a clock that also carries
  a wake_check keeps the probe's escalations (fire cap, deadline-only wakes; t_f6d930b7) and the stated-window
  exemption. The probeless tests no longer vary why to dodge escalation.
- A declared clock needs a non-empty why (invalid_awaiting); clock_only + wake_check gets a message saying
  clock_only names no producer.
- Goal loop: the CLI/gateway block_fn declares {kind:'clock', why:'goal judge: ...'} plus clock_only for a judge
  reason with SCHEDULED_UNTIL (before, the >2 h guard refused it and the card stayed running); park() passes the
  awaiting too (its goal_unachievable park is never timed).
- Only scheduled and blocked kind=time ledger cards lend park/awaiting/wake_check to replica rows; park_fields
  accepts +HHMM offsets.
- Tests that park on main since the rebase (pr_replica_comment_uid, review_model_cycles) and those declaring a
  bare {kind:'clock'} (soak_wait, triage_park) declare a why.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
